<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">In this expression, <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the probability of producing a correct answer given the question <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> and a particular thinking trace <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒛</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{z}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The distribution <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\phi}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\phi}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> is the <span id="S2.SS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">variational posterior</span>, which conditions not only on the question <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> but also on an auxiliary <span id="S2.SS1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">answer hint</span> <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S2.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\phi}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=q_{\phi}\big([{\bm{z}},\texttt{&lt;/think&gt;}]\mid[{\bm{x}},\texttt{&lt;hint&gt;},{\bm{y}}^{\prime},\texttt{&lt;/hint&gt;},\texttt{&lt;think&gt;}]\big)\textrm{.}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">&lt;/think&gt;</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">&lt;hint&gt;</mtext><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">&lt;/hint&gt;</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">&lt;think&gt;</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>.</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\phi}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=q_{\phi}\big([{\bm{z}},\texttt{&lt;/think&gt;}]\mid[{\bm{x}},\texttt{&lt;hint&gt;},{\bm{y}}^{\prime},\texttt{&lt;/hint&gt;},\texttt{&lt;think&gt;}]\big)\textrm{.}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Here, <span id="S2.SS1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;hint&gt;</span> and <span id="S2.SS1.p1.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;/hint&gt;</span> are shown as example delimiters; in experiments, we ablate different special tokens to wrap the hint <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and concatenate it after <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Conditioning on <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> encourages the variational posterior to generate thinking traces <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒛</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{z}}</annotation></semantics></math> that are more likely to yield correct answers. A simple yet effective design choice is to let <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> come directly from the oracle set, that is, <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{supp}[q_{\phi}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})]\subset\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{supp}[q_{\phi}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})]\subset\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. In practice, <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> may be a rephrasing of a reference answer or any correct expression sampled from <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We can further show (detailed in Appendix <a href="#A1.SS1" title="A.1 Derivation for Eq. () ‣ Appendix A Detailed derivations ‣ Variational Reasoning for Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>) that maximizing the ELBO objective w.r.t. <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq. (<a href="#S2.E2" title="In 2.1 Evidence lower bound ‣ 2 Variational reasoning ‣ Variational Reasoning for Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) is equivalent to minimizing the <em id="S2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">reverse</em> KL divergence between <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\phi}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\phi}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}})</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S2.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\textrm{ELBO}}({\bm{x}},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime};\pi_{\theta},q_{\phi})=\log P_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})-{\color[rgb]{0,0,1}\mathbb{D}_{\textrm{KL}}\left(q_{\phi}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})||P_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}})\right)}\textrm{.}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>ELBO</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">𝔻</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">ϕ</mi></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" fence="false" mathcolor="#0000FF" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">,</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">𝒚</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">′</mo></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" fence="false" mathcolor="#0000FF" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" fence="false" mathcolor="#0000FF" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">P</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" fence="false" mathcolor="#0000FF" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#0000FF">𝒴</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">𝒙</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF">)</mo></mrow><mtext>.</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\textrm{ELBO}}({\bm{x}},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime};\pi_{\theta},q_{\phi})=\log P_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})-{\color[rgb]{0,0,1}\mathbb{D}_{\textrm{KL}}\left(q_{\phi}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})||P_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}})\right)}\textrm{.}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Here <span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS1.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="16.6" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.84px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 224.29 16.6" width="224.29"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,16.6) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.15 L 0 12.45 C 0 14.75 1.86 16.6 4.15 16.6 L 220.14 16.6 C 222.43 16.6 224.29 14.75 224.29 12.45 L 224.29 4.15 C 224.29 1.86 222.43 0 220.14 0 L 4.15 0 C 1.86 0 0 1.86 0 4.15 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#EDEDED;" fill="#EDEDED" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.15 L 0 12.45 C 0 14.75 1.86 16.6 4.15 16.6 L 220.14 16.6 C 222.43 16.6 224.29 14.75 224.29 12.45 L 224.29 4.15 C 224.29 1.86 222.43 0 220.14 0 L 4.15 0 C 1.86 0 0 1.86 0 4.15 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 2.77 4.84)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:15.81em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="218.76"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S2.SS1.p2.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}})=\frac{\pi_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})}{P_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒴</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒴</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒴</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}})=\frac{\pi_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})}{P_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span> is the <span id="S2.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">true posterior</span>. Compared with the prior distribution <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math>, this posterior distribution re-weights thinking traces by <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})</annotation></semantics></math>, thus favoring <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒛</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{z}}</annotation></semantics></math> that are more likely to produce correct answers. According to Eq. (<a href="#S2.E4" title="In 2.1 Evidence lower bound ‣ 2 Variational reasoning ‣ Variational Reasoning for Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>), we know that the optimal solution for <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{q_{\phi}}\mathcal{L}_{\textrm{ELBO}}({\bm{x}},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime};\pi_{\theta},q_{\phi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>ELBO</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{q_{\phi}}\mathcal{L}_{\textrm{ELBO}}({\bm{x}},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime};\pi_{\theta},q_{\phi})</annotation></semantics></math> is: <span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS1.p2.pic2" class="ltx_picture" height="17.13" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-5.34px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 286.42 17.13" width="286.42"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,17.13) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.15 L 0 12.98 C 0 15.27 1.86 17.13 4.15 17.13 L 282.27 17.13 C 284.56 17.13 286.42 15.27 286.42 12.98 L 286.42 4.15 C 286.42 1.86 284.56 0 282.27 0 L 4.15 0 C 1.86 0 0 1.86 0 4.15 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#EDEDED;" fill="#EDEDED" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.15 L 0 12.98 C 0 15.27 1.86 17.13 4.15 17.13 L 282.27 17.13 C 284.56 17.13 286.42 15.27 286.42 12.98 L 286.42 4.15 C 286.42 1.86 284.56 0 282.27 0 L 4.15 0 C 1.86 0 0 1.86 0 4.15 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 2.77 5.34)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:9.39em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="14.36" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.4)" width="129.97"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S2.SS1.p2.pic2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\sim q_{\phi}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒚</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒚</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall{\bm{y}}^{\prime}\sim q_{\phi}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p2.pic2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, there is <math id="S2.SS1.p2.pic2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\phi}^{*}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=P_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒚</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒴</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\phi}^{*}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})=P_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}})</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.2 </span>Extension to IWAE-style lower bound</h3>

<div id="S2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In reinforcement learning (RL), it is now common practice to perform parallel rollouts of multiple thinking traces <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒛</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{z}}</annotation></semantics></math> and answers <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒚</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}</annotation></semantics></math> for a given question <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shao et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. This naturally motivates us to extend the single-trace ELBO in Eq. (<a href="#S2.E4" title="In 2.1 Evidence lower bound ‣ 2 Variational reasoning ‣ Variational Reasoning for Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) to an importance-weighted autoencoder (IWAE) style bound <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Burda et al., 2015</a>)</cite>. By leveraging multiple <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> traces, this approach yields a strictly tighter lower bound. Specifically, we obtain the following <em id="S2.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">IWAE-style lower bound</em> for <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log P_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log P_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S2.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\textrm{ELBO}}^{K}({\bm{x}},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime};\pi_{\theta},q_{\phi})=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{z}}_{1:K}\sim q_{\phi}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})}\left[\log\frac{1}{K}\sum_{k=1}^{K}\frac{\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}_{k},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})}{q_{\phi}({\bm{z}}_{k}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})}\right]\textrm{.}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>ELBO</mtext><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow><mtext>.</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\textrm{ELBO}}^{K}({\bm{x}},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime};\pi_{\theta},q_{\phi})=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{z}}_{1:K}\sim q_{\phi}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})}\left[\log\frac{1}{K}\sum_{k=1}^{K}\frac{\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}_{k},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})}{q_{\phi}({\bm{z}}_{k}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})}\right]\textrm{.}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">These IWAE-style bounds satisfy <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\textrm{ELBO}}^{K}\leq\mathcal{L}_{\textrm{ELBO}}^{K+1}\leq\log P_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>ELBO</mtext><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>ELBO</mtext><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\textrm{ELBO}}^{K}\leq\mathcal{L}_{\textrm{ELBO}}^{K+1}\leq\log P_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\in\mathbb{N}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℕ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\in\mathbb{N}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, which means the bound becomes tighter as <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> increases (the proof is similar to that of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Burda et al. (2015)</a></cite>). The single-trace ELBO objective in Eq. (<a href="#S2.E4" title="In 2.1 Evidence lower bound ‣ 2 Variational reasoning ‣ Variational Reasoning for Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) corresponds to the special case of <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=1</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\textrm{ELBO}}=\mathcal{L}_{\textrm{ELBO}}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>ELBO</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>ELBO</mtext><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\textrm{ELBO}}=\mathcal{L}_{\textrm{ELBO}}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Gradient estimation.</span> We now derive the gradient of <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\textrm{ELBO}}^{K}({\bm{x}},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime};\pi_{\theta},q_{\phi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>ELBO</mtext><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\textrm{ELBO}}^{K}({\bm{x}},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime};\pi_{\theta},q_{\phi})</annotation></semantics></math> w.r.t. the model parameters <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> (see Appendix <a href="#A1.SS2" title="A.2 Derivation for Eq. () ‣ Appendix A Detailed derivations ‣ Variational Reasoning for Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a> for the gradient w.r.t. the variational parameters <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\phi}\mathcal{L}_{\textrm{ELBO}}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>ELBO</mtext><mi>K</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\phi}\mathcal{L}_{\textrm{ELBO}}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>):</p>
<table id="S2.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}&amp;\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\textrm{ELBO}}^{K}({\bm{x}},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime};\pi_{\theta},q_{\phi})=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{z}}_{1:K}\sim q_{\phi}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})}\left[\sum_{k=1}^{K}\widetilde{\rho}_{k}\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}_{k},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})\right]\textrm{,}\\
&amp;\textrm{where}\quad\widetilde{\rho}_{k}=\frac{\rho_{k}}{\sum_{j=1}^{K}\rho_{j}}\quad\text{and}\quad\rho_{k}=\frac{\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}_{k},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})}{q_{\phi}({\bm{z}}_{k}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})}\textrm{.}\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>ELBO</mtext></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>K</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>K</mi></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>]</mo><mtext>,</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>where</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mspace style="width:2.000em;" width="2.000em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:2.000em;" width="2.000em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>.</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}&amp;\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\textrm{ELBO}}^{K}({\bm{x}},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime};\pi_{\theta},q_{\phi})=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{z}}_{1:K}\sim q_{\phi}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})}\left[\sum_{k=1}^{K}\widetilde{\rho}_{k}\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}_{k},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})\right]\textrm{,}\\
&amp;\textrm{where}\quad\widetilde{\rho}_{k}=\frac{\rho_{k}}{\sum_{j=1}^{K}\rho_{j}}\quad\text{and}\quad\rho_{k}=\frac{\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}_{k},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})}{q_{\phi}({\bm{z}}_{k}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})}\textrm{.}\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Estimating <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span> The weight <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq. (<a href="#S2.E6" title="In 2.2 Extension to IWAE-style lower bound ‣ 2 Variational reasoning ‣ Variational Reasoning for Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) can be decomposed as <span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS2.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="16.6" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.84px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 208.16 16.6" width="208.16"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,16.6) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.15 L 0 12.45 C 0 14.75 1.86 16.6 4.15 16.6 L 204 16.6 C 206.3 16.6 208.16 14.75 208.16 12.45 L 208.16 4.15 C 208.16 1.86 206.3 0 204 0 L 4.15 0 C 1.86 0 0 1.86 0 4.15 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#EDEDED;" fill="#EDEDED" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.15 L 0 12.45 C 0 14.75 1.86 16.6 4.15 16.6 L 204 16.6 C 206.3 16.6 208.16 14.75 208.16 12.45 L 208.16 4.15 C 208.16 1.86 206.3 0 204 0 L 4.15 0 C 1.86 0 0 1.86 0 4.15 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 2.77 4.84)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:14.64em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="202.62"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S2.SS2.p2.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{k}=\frac{\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}_{k}|{\bm{x}})}{q_{\phi}({\bm{z}}_{k}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})}\cdot\pi_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}}_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ρ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒚</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒴</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{k}=\frac{\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}_{k}|{\bm{x}})}{q_{\phi}({\bm{z}}_{k}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})}\cdot\pi_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}}_{k})</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>, where the first term, <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}_{k}|{\bm{x}})}{q_{\phi}({\bm{z}}_{k}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}_{k}|{\bm{x}})}{q_{\phi}({\bm{z}}_{k}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})}</annotation></semantics></math>, is the <em id="S2.SS2.p2.2.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">likelihood ratio of the thinking trace</em> <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{z}}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{z}}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the second term, <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}}_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}}_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>, is the probability of producing a correct answer given <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{z}}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{z}}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. In reasoning models, a single trace <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{z}}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{z}}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> may contain thousands of tokens. Directly computing the likelihood ratio over such long sequences often leads to high variance, a phenomenon also reported in concurrent studies <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cetin et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib75" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zheng et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. To mitigate this issue, we use the geometric mean <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(\tfrac{\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}_{k}|{\bm{x}})}{q_{\phi}({\bm{z}}_{k}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})}\big)^{1/|{\bm{z}}_{k}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(\tfrac{\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}_{k}|{\bm{x}})}{q_{\phi}({\bm{z}}_{k}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})}\big)^{1/|{\bm{z}}_{k}|}</annotation></semantics></math> as a surrogate for the likelihood ratio of <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{z}}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{z}}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. This per-token normalization reduces variance at the cost of introducing some bias, effectively spreading the ratio evenly across the thinking tokens.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Training pipeline of variational reasoning</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
              
              
            An initial reasoning model <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta_{0}}({\bm{z}},{\bm{y}}|{\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta_{0}}({\bm{z}},{\bm{y}}|{\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math>, variational posterior <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\phi}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\phi}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, question-answer dataset <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}^{*}_{{\bm{x}}}\}\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}^{*}_{{\bm{x}}}\}\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}^{*}_{{\bm{x}}}\in\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}^{*}_{{\bm{x}}}\in\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is one of the reference answers corresponding to <math id="alg1.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
              
              
            Rollout numbers <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="alg1.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>, training rounds <math id="alg1.l2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, steps per round <math id="alg1.l2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="alg1.l2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math>, optimizer <math id="alg1.l2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
              
              
            The trained model parameters <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> and variational parameters <math id="alg1.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
              
              
