</figure>
<div id="S2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">As for computing <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}}_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}}_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>, we consider two unbiased estimators: <span id="S2.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(i)</span> <span id="S2.SS2.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">likelihood-based estimator</span> is <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})=|\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}}|\cdot\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{y}}\sim\mathcal{U}(\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}})}\left[\pi_{\theta}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})=|\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}}|\cdot\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{y}}\sim\mathcal{U}(\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}})}\left[\pi_{\theta}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})\right]</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}}|</annotation></semantics></math> is cardinality of <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}(\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}(\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> is the uniform distribution on <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>; <span id="S2.SS2.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(ii)</span> <span id="S2.SS2.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">accuracy-based estimator</span> is <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{y}}\sim\pi_{\theta}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})}\left[\mathds{1}({\bm{y}}\in\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{y}}\sim\pi_{\theta}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})}\left[\mathds{1}({\bm{y}}\in\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}})\right]</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathds{1}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathds{1}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is the indicator function. When <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}}|=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}}|=1</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., there is a unique correct answer expression <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib77" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhou et al. (2025)</a></cite> show that the likelihood-based estimator has lower variance (in fact, zero) compared to the accuracy-based one. We now extend this comparison to general cases when <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}}|&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}}|&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(Proof in Appendix <a href="#A1.SS3" title="A.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Detailed derivations ‣ Variational Reasoning for Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a>) For <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}}|&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}}|&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, the worst-case variances of the likelihood-based estimator and the accuracy-based estimator over all possible <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> (under fixed <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐳</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})</annotation></semantics></math>) are</span></p>
<table id="S2.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{\pi_{\theta}}\textrm{Var}_{\textrm{like}}=\left(|\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}}|-1\right)\cdot\pi_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})^{2}\textnormal{;}\quad\max_{\pi_{\theta}}\textrm{Var}_{\textrm{acc}}=\pi_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})\cdot\left(1-\pi_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})\right)\textrm{.}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Var</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">like</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>;</mtext></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Var</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">acc</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">.</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{\pi_{\theta}}\textrm{Var}_{\textrm{like}}=\left(|\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}}|-1\right)\cdot\pi_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})^{2}\textnormal{;}\quad\max_{\pi_{\theta}}\textrm{Var}_{\textrm{acc}}=\pi_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})\cdot\left(1-\pi_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})\right)\textrm{.}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Therefore, the accuracy-based estimator has lower worst-case variance, i.e., <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{\pi_{\theta}}\textrm{Var}_{\textrm{acc}}\leq\max_{\pi_{\theta}}\textrm{Var}_{\textrm{like}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Var</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">acc</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Var</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">like</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{\pi_{\theta}}\textrm{Var}_{\textrm{acc}}\leq\max_{\pi_{\theta}}\textrm{Var}_{\textrm{like}}</annotation></semantics></math>, whenever the model accuracy (conditional on <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}}</annotation></semantics></math>) satisfies <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})\geq\frac{1}{|\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐳</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})\geq\frac{1}{|\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}}|}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Note that for many practical questions, the space of correct answers can be quite flexible, so typically <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}}|\gg 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≫</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}}|\gg 1</annotation></semantics></math>. In this regime, the accuracy-based estimator enjoys much lower worst-case variance. Based on this insight, in our experiments we estimate the weight <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<table id="S2.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{k}^{\textrm{est}}=\big(\tfrac{\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}_{k}|{\bm{x}})}{q_{\phi}({\bm{z}}_{k}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})}\big)^{1/|{\bm{z}}_{k}|}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{y}}\sim\pi_{\theta}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}}_{k})}\left[\mathds{1}({\bm{y}}\in\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}})\right]\textrm{,}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>k</mi><mtext>est</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>,</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{k}^{\textrm{est}}=\big(\tfrac{\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}_{k}|{\bm{x}})}{q_{\phi}({\bm{z}}_{k}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})}\big)^{1/|{\bm{z}}_{k}|}\cdot\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{y}}\sim\pi_{\theta}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}}_{k})}\left[\mathds{1}({\bm{y}}\in\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}})\right]\textrm{,}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where the expectation <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{y}}\sim\pi_{\theta}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}}_{k})}\left[\mathds{1}({\bm{y}}\in\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{y}}\sim\pi_{\theta}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}}_{k})}\left[\mathds{1}({\bm{y}}\in\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}})\right]</annotation></semantics></math> is approximated by sampling multiple candidate answers for each thinking trace <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{z}}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{z}}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, similar to the implementation in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">Qi et al. (2025)</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Estimating <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}_{k},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}_{k},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span> When evaluating <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\textrm{ELBO}}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>ELBO</mtext><mi>K</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\textrm{ELBO}}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq. (<a href="#S2.E6" title="In 2.2 Extension to IWAE-style lower bound ‣ 2 Variational reasoning ‣ Variational Reasoning for Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>), we need the gradient <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}_{k},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})=\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}_{k}|{\bm{x}})+\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}}_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}_{k},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})=\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}_{k}|{\bm{x}})+\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}}_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>. The first term, <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}_{k}|{\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}_{k}|{\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math>, is straightforward to calculate. For the second term, <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}}_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}}_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>, we also adopt an <em id="S2.SS2.p5.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">accuracy-based estimator</em>: <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}}_{k})=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{y}}\sim\pi_{\theta}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}}_{k})}\left[\mathds{1}({\bm{y}}\in\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}})\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}}_{k})\right]}{\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{y}}\sim\pi_{\theta}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}}_{k})}\left[\mathds{1}({\bm{y}}\in\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}})\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}}_{k})=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{y}}\sim\pi_{\theta}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}}_{k})}\left[\mathds{1}({\bm{y}}\in\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}})\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}}_{k})\right]}{\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{y}}\sim\pi_{\theta}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}}_{k})}\left[\mathds{1}({\bm{y}}\in\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}})\right]}</annotation></semantics></math>. In practice, the expectations w.r.t. <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}}_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}}_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> are approximated using the same samples drawn to estimate <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{k}^{\mathrm{est}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>est</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{k}^{\mathrm{est}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.3 </span>Optimizing the variational posterior via forward KL divergence</h3>

<div id="S2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">While Eq. (<a href="#S2.E5" title="In 2.2 Extension to IWAE-style lower bound ‣ 2 Variational reasoning ‣ Variational Reasoning for Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) provides IWAE-style bounds that yield tighter optimization of the MLE objective w.r.t. the model parameters <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> (through <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{ELBO}}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>ELBO</mi><mi>K</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{ELBO}}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>), our pilot experiments show unexpected behavior for the optimization of the variational parameters <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> (through <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\phi}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{ELBO}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>ELBO</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\phi}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{ELBO}}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\phi}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{ELBO}}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>ELBO</mi><mi>K</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\phi}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{ELBO}}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>). Recall from Eq. (<a href="#S2.E4" title="In 2.1 Evidence lower bound ‣ 2 Variational reasoning ‣ Variational Reasoning for Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) that the ELBO objective minimizes the <em id="S2.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">reverse</em> KL divergence <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{D}_{\textrm{KL}}\left(q_{\phi}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})||P_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{D}_{\textrm{KL}}\left(q_{\phi}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})||P_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}})\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, where both the expectation and Monte Carlo samples are taken under <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\phi}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\phi}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>. In practice, however, the policy model <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> is often already well-trained due to pretraining of base LLMs <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, while the variational posterior <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\phi}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\phi}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> may <em id="S2.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">struggle to effectively use hints <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> from correct answers without collapsing into shortcut reasoning</em> (e.g., directly leaking answer tokens into the thinking trace). To address this imbalance, we propose to optimize <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\phi}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\phi}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> using the <em id="S2.SS3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">forward</em> KL divergence <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{D}_{\textrm{KL}}(P_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}})||q_{\phi}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;" mathcolor="#FF8000">𝔻</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;" mathcolor="#FF8000">KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;" mathcolor="#FF8000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;" mathcolor="#FF8000">P</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;" mathcolor="#FF8000">θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;" mathcolor="#FF8000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;" mathcolor="#FF8000">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#FF8000" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;" mathcolor="#FF8000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;" mathcolor="#FF8000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF8000">𝒴</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;" mathcolor="#FF8000">𝒙</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;" mathcolor="#FF8000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#FF8000" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#FF8000" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;" mathcolor="#FF8000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;" mathcolor="#FF8000">ϕ</mi></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;" mathcolor="#FF8000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;" mathcolor="#FF8000">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#FF8000" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;" mathcolor="#FF8000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;" mathcolor="#FF8000">,</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;" mathcolor="#FF8000">𝒚</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;" mathcolor="#FF8000">′</mo></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;" mathcolor="#FF8000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF8000;" mathcolor="#FF8000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{D}_{\textrm{KL}}(P_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}})||q_{\phi}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}))</annotation></semantics></math>, whose gradient w.r.t. <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> can be written as:<span id="footnote2" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">2</span>
              
              
              
            We assume that <math id="footnote2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\phi}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\phi}({\bm{y}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> is a fixed prior distribution and does not involve gradients.</span></span></span></p>
<table id="S2.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\!\!\!&amp;\nabla_{\phi}\mathbb{D}_{\textrm{KL}}(P_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}})||q_{\phi}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}))\simeq\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{z}}_{1:M}\sim\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})}\!\!\left[\sum_{m=1}^{M}\!\widetilde{w}_{m}\nabla_{\phi}\log q_{\phi}({\bm{z}}_{m}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\right]\triangleq\nabla_{\phi}\mathcal{L}_{\textrm{forward}}^{M}\textrm{,}\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\\
\!\!\!&amp;\textrm{where}\quad\widetilde{w}_{m}=\frac{w_{m}}{\sum_{j=1}^{M}w_{j}}\quad\text{and}\quad w_{m}=\pi_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}}_{m})=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{y}}\sim\pi_{\theta}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}}_{m})}\left[\mathds{1}({\bm{y}}\in\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}})\right]\textrm{.}\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mi>𝔻</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>≃</mo><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>M</mi></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>]</mo><mo>≜</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>forward</mtext></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>M</mi></msup><mtext>,</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>where</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mspace style="width:2.000em;" width="2.000em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:2.000em;" width="2.000em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒛</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>.</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\!\!\!&amp;\nabla_{\phi}\mathbb{D}_{\textrm{KL}}(P_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}})||q_{\phi}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime}))\simeq\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{z}}_{1:M}\sim\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})}\!\!\left[\sum_{m=1}^{M}\!\widetilde{w}_{m}\nabla_{\phi}\log q_{\phi}({\bm{z}}_{m}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})\right]\triangleq\nabla_{\phi}\mathcal{L}_{\textrm{forward}}^{M}\textrm{,}\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\\
\!\!\!&amp;\textrm{where}\quad\widetilde{w}_{m}=\frac{w_{m}}{\sum_{j=1}^{M}w_{j}}\quad\text{and}\quad w_{m}=\pi_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{\bm{x}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}}_{m})=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{y}}\sim\pi_{\theta}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}}_{m})}\left[\mathds{1}({\bm{y}}\in\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}})\right]\textrm{.}\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This approximation, <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\phi}\mathcal{L}_{\textrm{forward}}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>forward</mtext><mi>M</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\phi}\mathcal{L}_{\textrm{forward}}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, follows a derivation similar to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bornschein &amp; Bengio (2015)</a></cite> (see Appendix <a href="#A1.SS4" title="A.4 Derivation for Eq. () ‣ Appendix A Detailed derivations ‣ Variational Reasoning for Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.4</span></a>), with the sample size <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> not necessarily equal to <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> used in <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{ELBO}}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>ELBO</mi><mi>K</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{ELBO}}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>. Unlike IWAE, this objective is an approximation rather than a lower bound. Optimizing Eq. (<a href="#S2.E9" title="In 2.3 Optimizing the variational posterior via forward KL divergence ‣ 2 Variational reasoning ‣ Variational Reasoning for Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>) can be viewed as a weighted supervised finetuning (SFT) for <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\phi}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\phi}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{y}}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, where training data is sampled from <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We summarize the overall training pipeline of our variational reasoning method in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 2.2 Extension to IWAE-style lower bound ‣ 2 Variational reasoning ‣ Variational Reasoning for Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. In our experiments, we train for only a single round (<math id="S2.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=1</annotation></semantics></math>), leaving multi-round training as an interesting direction for future work.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>Connection to other methods</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In prior work, the thinking trace <math id="S3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒛</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{z}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the final answer <math id="S3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒚</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}</annotation></semantics></math> are often treated together as the full output in the formulations <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shao et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Guo et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib63" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. By explicitly decomposing the output into a thinking process <math id="S3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒛</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{z}}</annotation></semantics></math> and an answer <math id="S3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒚</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}</annotation></semantics></math>, as we have done above, we can gain fresh perspectives on how our formulation relates to other mainstream methods.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Connection to rejection sampling finetuning (RFT).</span> RFT methods <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dong et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">Touvron et al., 2023</a>)</cite> generate multiple candidate outputs for each input <math id="S3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> using a reference model <math id="S3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\textrm{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\textrm{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and then select the candidate with the highest reward. The reference model may be a strong teacher model or identical to the learner <math id="S3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., <math id="S3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\textrm{ref}}=\pi_{\theta}^{\mathrm{sg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>sg</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\textrm{ref}}=\pi_{\theta}^{\mathrm{sg}}</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="S3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{sg}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>sg</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{sg}</annotation></semantics></math> denoting stop-gradient). Formally, the gradient of RFT training objective, <em id="S3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">focusing only on the learning of the thinking trace <math id="S3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{z}}</annotation></semantics></math></em>, can be written as:</p>
<table id="S3.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\textrm{RFT}}({\bm{x}},\pi_{\theta})\triangleq{}&amp;\nabla_{\theta}\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})}\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})}\left[\mathds{1}({\bm{y}}\in\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}})\cdot\log\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}},{\bm{y}}|{\bm{x}})\right]\\
={}&amp;\nabla_{\theta}\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})}\left[\pi_{\textrm{ref}}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})\cdot\left(\log\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}}){\color[rgb]{0.668,0.668,0.668}{}+\log\pi_{\theta}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})}\right)\right]\\
\xRightarrow[\scriptstyle\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})]{\textrm{only w.r.t.}}{}&amp;\nabla_{\theta}\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})}\left[\pi_{\textrm{ref}}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})\cdot\log\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})\right]\\
={}&amp;-{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}P_{\textrm{ref}}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})}\cdot\nabla_{\theta}\mathbb{D}_{\textrm{KL}}(P_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}})||\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}}))\textrm{.}\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>RFT</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≜</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒛</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#AAAAAA;" mathcolor="#AAAAAA">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#AAAAAA;" mathcolor="#AAAAAA">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#AAAAAA;" mathcolor="#AAAAAA">π</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#AAAAAA;" mathcolor="#AAAAAA">θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#AAAAAA;" mathcolor="#AAAAAA" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#AAAAAA;" mathcolor="#AAAAAA">𝒚</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#AAAAAA;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#AAAAAA" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#AAAAAA;" mathcolor="#AAAAAA">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#AAAAAA;" mathcolor="#AAAAAA">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#AAAAAA;" mathcolor="#AAAAAA">𝒛</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#AAAAAA;" mathcolor="#AAAAAA" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathvariant="italic">⇒</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">π</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝒛</mi><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝒙</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mtext mathsize="0.700em">only w.r.t.</mtext></munderover></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">ref</mtext></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF0000">𝒴</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">𝒙</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#FF0000" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>𝔻</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mtext>.</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\textrm{RFT}}({\bm{x}},\pi_{\theta})\triangleq{}&amp;\nabla_{\theta}\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})}\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})}\left[\mathds{1}({\bm{y}}\in\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}})\cdot\log\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}},{\bm{y}}|{\bm{x}})\right]\\
={}&amp;\nabla_{\theta}\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})}\left[\pi_{\textrm{ref}}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})\cdot\left(\log\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}}){\color[rgb]{0.668,0.668,0.668}{}+\log\pi_{\theta}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})}\right)\right]\\
\xRightarrow[\scriptstyle\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})]{\textrm{only w.r.t.}}{}&amp;\nabla_{\theta}\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})}\left[\pi_{\textrm{ref}}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})\cdot\log\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})\right]\\
={}&amp;-{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}P_{\textrm{ref}}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})}\cdot\nabla_{\theta}\mathbb{D}_{\textrm{KL}}(P_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}})||\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}}))\textrm{.}\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Here <math id="S3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\textrm{ref}}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})=\sum_{{\bm{y}}\in\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}}P_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\textrm{ref}}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})=\sum_{{\bm{y}}\in\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}}P_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the <em id="S3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">model accuracy</em> on instruction <math id="S3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the true posterior of the reference model is <math id="S3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}})=\frac{\pi_{\textrm{ref}}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})\pi_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})}{P_{\textrm{ref}}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}})=\frac{\pi_{\textrm{ref}}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})\pi_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})}{P_{\textrm{ref}}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})}</annotation></semantics></math>. As seen, the RFT objective can be viewed as maximizing a forward KL divergence weighted by <math id="S3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\textrm{ref}}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\textrm{ref}}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math>, with the optimal solution <span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S3.p3.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="16.6" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.84px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 147.68 16.6" width="147.68"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,16.6) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.15 L 0 12.45 C 0 14.75 1.86 16.6 4.15 16.6 L 143.53 16.6 C 145.82 16.6 147.68 14.75 147.68 12.45 L 147.68 4.15 C 147.68 1.86 145.82 0 143.53 0 L 4.15 0 C 1.86 0 0 1.86 0 4.15 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#EDEDED;" fill="#EDEDED" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.15 L 0 12.45 C 0 14.75 1.86 16.6 4.15 16.6 L 143.53 16.6 C 145.82 16.6 147.68 14.75 147.68 12.45 L 147.68 4.15 C 147.68 1.86 145.82 0 143.53 0 L 4.15 0 C 1.86 0 0 1.86 0 4.15 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 2.77 4.84)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:10.27em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="142.14"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S3.p3.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}^{*}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})=P_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒛</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒴</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒙</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}^{*}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})=P_{\textrm{ref}}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}})</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>. In practice, this weighting downplays hard questions with small <math id="S3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\textrm{ref}}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\textrm{ref}}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math>, biasing training toward easier ones. In contrast, our formulation in Eq. (<a href="#S2.E9" title="In 2.3 Optimizing the variational posterior via forward KL divergence ‣ 2 Variational reasoning ‣ Variational Reasoning for Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>) treats all questions more evenly, ensuring that the objective remains attentive to difficult cases.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Connection to binary reward RL.</span> In the case of RL training with a 0–1 binary reward, the training objective can be written in a form similar to Eq. (<a href="#S3.E10" title="In 3 Connection to other methods ‣ Variational Reasoning for Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>), focusing only on the thinking trace <math id="S3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒛</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{z}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\textrm{bi-RL}}({\bm{x}},\pi_{\theta})\triangleq{}&amp;\nabla_{\theta}\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})}\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\theta}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})}\left[\mathds{1}({\bm{y}}\in\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}})\right]\\
\xRightarrow[\scriptstyle\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})]{\textrm{only w.r.t.}}{}&amp;\nabla_{\theta}\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\theta}^{\mathrm{sg}}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})}\left[\pi_{\theta}^{\mathrm{sg}}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})\cdot\log\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})\right]\\
={}&amp;-{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}P_{\theta}^{\mathrm{sg}}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})}\cdot\nabla_{\theta}\mathbb{D}_{\textrm{KL}}(P_{\theta}^{\mathrm{sg}}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}})||\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}}))\textrm{.}\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>bi-RL</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≜</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathvariant="italic">⇒</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">π</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝒛</mi><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝒙</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mtext mathsize="0.700em">only w.r.t.</mtext></munderover></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>sg</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>sg</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">θ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">sg</mi></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF0000">𝒴</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">𝒙</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#FF0000" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>𝔻</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>sg</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mtext>.</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\textrm{bi-RL}}({\bm{x}},\pi_{\theta})\triangleq{}&amp;\nabla_{\theta}\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})}\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\theta}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})}\left[\mathds{1}({\bm{y}}\in\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}})\right]\\
\xRightarrow[\scriptstyle\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})]{\textrm{only w.r.t.}}{}&amp;\nabla_{\theta}\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\theta}^{\mathrm{sg}}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})}\left[\pi_{\theta}^{\mathrm{sg}}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})\cdot\log\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})\right]\\
={}&amp;-{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}P_{\theta}^{\mathrm{sg}}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})}\cdot\nabla_{\theta}\mathbb{D}_{\textrm{KL}}(P_{\theta}^{\mathrm{sg}}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}})||\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}}))\textrm{.}\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, the local gradient for <math id="S3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> in binary-reward RL is equivalent to minimizing the forward KL divergence between <math id="S3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> and the true posterior <math id="S3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\theta}^{\mathrm{sg}}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}})=\frac{\pi_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})}{P_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>sg</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\theta}^{\mathrm{sg}}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}})=\frac{\pi_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})}{P_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})}</annotation></semantics></math>, with the update further weighted by the model accuracy <math id="S3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\theta}^{\mathrm{sg}}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>sg</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\theta}^{\mathrm{sg}}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math>. Interestingly, the RL training objective itself is <math id="S3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\textrm{bi-RL}}({\bm{x}},\pi_{\theta})=\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})}\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\theta}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})}\left[\mathds{1}({\bm{y}}\in\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}})\right]=P_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>bi-RL</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒛</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\textrm{bi-RL}}({\bm{x}},\pi_{\theta})=\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})}\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\theta}({\bm{y}}|{\bm{x}},{\bm{z}})}\left[\mathds{1}({\bm{y}}\in\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}})\right]=P_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math>, whereas the MLE objective in Eq. (<a href="#S2.E2" title="In 2.1 Evidence lower bound ‣ 2 Variational reasoning ‣ Variational Reasoning for Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) for our variational reasoning framework instead maximizes <math id="S3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log P_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log P_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Furthermore, in Group Relative Policy Optimization <span id="S3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(GRPO)</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shao et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, one of the most widely used RL training objectives, the reward is normalized by the standard deviation of rewards within a group of rollouts. Under 0–1 binary reward, each rollout reward follows a Bernoulli distribution with mean <math id="S3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> and standard deviation <math id="S3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{P_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})\cdot(1-P_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}}))}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{P_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})\cdot(1-P_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}}))}</annotation></semantics></math>. The gradient of the GRPO objective can therefore be derived as (we omit the <math id="S3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>min</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min</annotation></semantics></math> and clip operations for brevity)</p>
<table id="S3.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\textrm{bi-GRPO}}({\bm{x}},\pi_{\theta})\xRightarrow[\scriptstyle\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})]{\textrm{only w.r.t.}}-{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\sqrt{\frac{P_{\theta}^{\mathrm{sg}}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})}{1-P_{\theta}^{\mathrm{sg}}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})}}}\cdot\nabla_{\theta}\mathbb{D}_{\textrm{KL}}(P_{\theta}^{\mathrm{sg}}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}})||\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}}))\textrm{,}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>bi-GRPO</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathvariant="italic" rspace="0em">⇒</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">π</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝒛</mi><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝒙</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mtext mathsize="0.700em">only w.r.t.</mtext></munderover><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000"><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">P</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">θ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">sg</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF0000">𝒴</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">𝒙</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#FF0000" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">P</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">θ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">sg</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#FF0000">𝒴</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">𝒙</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#FF0000" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">𝒙</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>sg</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mtext>,</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\textrm{bi-GRPO}}({\bm{x}},\pi_{\theta})\xRightarrow[\scriptstyle\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})]{\textrm{only w.r.t.}}-{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\sqrt{\frac{P_{\theta}^{\mathrm{sg}}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})}{1-P_{\theta}^{\mathrm{sg}}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})}}}\cdot\nabla_{\theta}\mathbb{D}_{\textrm{KL}}(P_{\theta}^{\mathrm{sg}}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}})||\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}}))\textrm{,}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p7.1" class="ltx_p">which follows from <math id="S3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\textrm{bi-GRPO}}({\bm{x}},\pi_{\theta})=\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\textrm{bi-RL}}({\bm{x}},\pi_{\theta})/\sqrt{P_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})\cdot(1-P_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}}))}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>bi-GRPO</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>bi-RL</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\textrm{bi-GRPO}}({\bm{x}},\pi_{\theta})=\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\textrm{bi-RL}}({\bm{x}},\pi_{\theta})/\sqrt{P_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})\cdot(1-P_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}}))}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, the local gradient for <math id="S3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> in GRPO is still equivalent to minimizing the forward KL divergence between <math id="S3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> and the true posterior <math id="S3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\theta}^{\mathrm{sg}}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>sg</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\theta}^{\mathrm{sg}}({\bm{z}}|{\bm{x}},\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}})</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that the per-instruction weight becomes <math id="S3.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{P_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})/(1-P_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}}))}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{P_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})/(1-P_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}}))}</annotation></semantics></math>, which increases monotonically with model accuracy and therefore also emphasizes easier questions with higher <math id="S3.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>𝒙</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\theta}(\mathcal{Y}_{{\bm{x}}}|{\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math>. In Appendix <a href="#A1.SS5" title="A.5 Connection to more general RL reward shaping ‣ Appendix A Detailed derivations ‣ Variational Reasoning for Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.5</span></a>, we extend these analyses and derive gradients for more general RL reward shaping, including cases with a <em id="S3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">format reward</em>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Experiments</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Datasets.</span> We train on the Bespoke-Stratos-17k dataset curated by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al. (2025a)</a></cite>, which combines math problems from Numina-Math <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2024</a>)</cite> with code problems from APPS <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hendrycks et al., 2021a</a>)</cite> and TACO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2023</a>)</cite>. The dataset contains 16,710 samples, each paired with a long-thinking trace generated by DeepSeek-R1 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Guo et al., 2025</a>)</cite> or QwQ-32B-Preview <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">Team, 2024</a>)</cite>. To ensure fair evaluation, all training data is strictly separated from the test sets.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span>Performance of models trained from <span id="S4.T1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Qwen3-4B-Base</span>. All models are trained on Bespoke-Stratos-17k except for General-Reasoner-4B. The best and second-best results are highlighted using <span id="S4.T1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">bold text</span> and <span id="S4.T1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">underlined text</span>, respectively.</figcaption>
